Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 22:10:49 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 27/31] fix: focus peaking works - metre band with the engine
 depth constant, sampled depth, guide legend text

Peaking was invisible for three independent reasons: a near=far=0 band degenerated smoothstep to 0, the depth target was Load()ed with display-resolution coordinates, and (after a first fix) a CPU-side far-plane normalisation did not match the value the linear depth target uses, landing the band in the near out-of-focus zone. Band now travels in metres and the shader converts depth with PS_NearFarClipDist.y like CompositeDofPS; depth is sampled by UV; the band is pushed every frame. r_LensPeakingDebug 1/2 added (solid in-focus mask / depth ramp). Frame guides gain a legend: aspect label at the guide band and a focal / stop / focus / sensor readout. User-verified.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017nykaDjTHxHDSo11CsYx6M
